    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass, including the new `Cp50Tests` idempotency test. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint now honours an `Idempotency-Key` header: a repeated create with an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with **200**, instead of creating a duplicate (which the identity check would otherwise reject with 409).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor conventions (function-per-step, escalation handlers rather than flows \u2014 flows were unused in the repo):\n\n**New function classes** (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a `@Component` singleton mapping key \u2192 created owner id (`putIfAbsent`, first-writer-wins).\n- `RequireIdempotentCreate` \u2014 the new **first** pipeline step. Reads `@HttpHeaderParameter(\"Idempotency-Key\")` (null when absent, so ordinary creates are unaffected). If the key was already seen, it loads the owner, maps it to a DTO *while the governing transaction is still open*, and throws `OwnerIdempotentReplayException` to short-circuit. No/unseen key falls through via `next: require`.\n- `RecordIdempotentCreate` \u2014 runs after `save`/`audit`, once the owner has its persisted id, recording the key.\n\n**New escalation** (`rest/escalation/`):\n- `OwnerIdempotentReplayException` (checked, carries the `OwnerDto`) + `OwnerIdempotentReplayExceptionHandler` responding `200 ResponseEntity.ok(dto)`, plus its YAML in `officefloor/escalation/`.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`): inserted `idempotency` as the entry step (`next: require`) and `recordIdempotency` between `audit` and `respond`, both with `govern: [ transaction ]` to match the rest of the pipeline.\n\nKey design points: a missing header resolves to `null` (verified in OfficeFloor's `HttpArgumentManagedObjectSource`), so no other endpoint behaviour changes; the replay's DTO is built inside the open transaction so the handler never touches the persistence layer; and the key is only recorded on a successful create, so a rejected create can be retried.",
