    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`. Every step in `owners.POST.yml` runs inside one shared `transaction` governance, so all the writes below commit together at the very end (or roll back as a unit). Marking each as **[validate]** (can reject) or **[effect]** (mutation/derivation/persistence).\n\n## Gate (before the pipeline)\n- **[validate] Authorization** \u2014 the file declares `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`; without that role the request is rejected before any step runs.\n\n## Pipeline, in order\n\n1. **`idempotency` \u2014 RequireIdempotentCreate** [validate/short-circuit]\n   Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If the key was already recorded *and* that owner still exists, it maps that owner to a DTO and throws `OwnerIdempotentReplayException` \u2192 **200 replay**, short-circuiting the whole create (so a repeat never becomes a 409). No key / first-time key / vanished owner \u2192 falls through.\n\n2. **`require` \u2014 RequireOwnerFields** [validate]\n   Rejects **400** (`OwnerFieldsMissingException`, with an `errors` array naming each field) if any required field is missing/blank: `firstName`, `lastName`, address (needs a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** flat `address`, tested *after* normalization), `city`, `telephone`. On success publishes the validated body for later steps.\n\n3. **`registrationDate` \u2014 RequireRegistrationDateNotFuture** [validate]\n   If `registrationDate` is supplied and is after today \u2192 **400** (`OwnerRegistrationDateInvalidException`). Absent is allowed.\n\n4. **`postcode` \u2014 RequireOwnerPostcode** [validate]\n   If `postcode` is supplied: must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region it must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else **400** (`OwnerPostcodeInvalidException`). Absent is allowed.\n\n5. **`normalizeAddress` \u2014 NormalizeOwnerAddress** [effect]\n   Rewrites the address in place: trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. If structured `addressLine1` was given, normalizes the lines and composes the flat `address` from them.\n\n6. **`normalize` \u2014 NormalizeOwnerTelephone** [validate + effect]\n   Converts `telephone` to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; assume `+61` and drop a leading `0` when no country code; enforce 8\u201315 digits, with `+61`\u21929 and `+1`\u219210 national digits). Unconvertible \u2192 **400** (`OwnerTelephoneInvalidException`). Otherwise writes the E.164 value back.\n\n7. **`normalizeEmail` \u2014 NormalizeOwnerEmail** [validate + effect]\n   If `email` present: must match the email regex \u2192 else **400** (`OwnerEmailInvalidException`); on success lower-cases it in place. Absent/blank skipped.\n\n8. **`nonDisposableEmail` \u2014 RequireNonDisposableOwnerEmail** [validate]\n   If the email domain is in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400** (`OwnerEmailDisposableException`).\n\n9. **`cityCapacity` \u2014 RequireOwnerCityCapacity** [validate]\n   If the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive count over `findAll()`) \u2192 **409** (`OwnerCityCapacityExceededException`).\n\n10. **`dailyLimit` \u2014 RequireDailyOwnerLimit** [validate]\n    Computes the effective business day; if \u2265 100 owners already have that `registrationDate` \u2192 **429** (`OwnerDailyLimitExceededException`).\n\n11. **`build` \u2014 BuildOwner** [effect]\n    Maps the body to a new `Owner`; sets `registrationDate` to the effective business-day-adjusted date (defaults to today if absent, then rolls Sat/Sun/public-holiday forward to the next business day).\n\n12. **`assignCode` \u2014 AssignCustomerCode** [effect]\n    Sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>` where REGION is derived from postcode (falling back to city, else `UNKNOWN`) and HASH8 is the first 8 hex chars of `SHA-256(telephone + lastName)`. On collision with an existing code, appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 (smallest free).\n\n13. **`assignHousehold` \u2014 AssignHouseholdId** [effect]\n    Sets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode)`.\n\n14. **`requireHousehold` \u2014 RequireUniqueOwnerHousehold** [validate]\n    Unless the request set `sharesHousehold: true`, rejects **409** (`OwnerHouseholdDuplicateException`) if any existing non-deleted owner shares this `householdId`.\n\n15. **`identity` \u2014 RequireUniqueOwnerIdentity** [validate]\n    Rejects **409** (`OwnerIdentityDuplicateException`) if the whole `identityKey` (`E.164 telephone | lower-cased email | householdId`) exactly matches an existing non-deleted owner.\n\n16. **`assignHouseholdSize` \u2014 AssignHouseholdSize** [effect]\n    Sets `householdSize` = existing members with the same `householdId` + 1 (1 when no household).\n\n17. **`assignNamesakeCount` \u2014 AssignNamesakeCount** [effect]\n    Sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n18. **`assignMembership` \u2014 AssignMembershipNumber** [effect]\n    Sets `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of the registration date's fiscal-year start year).\n\n19. **`assignMembershipLevel` \u2014 AssignMembershipLevel** [effect]\n    Computes `membershipPoints` (base 0; +2 email present; +1 `namesakeCount==0`; +2 `householdSize\u22653`; +3 tenure \u2265 1 fiscal year \u2014 never at creation) and maps to `membershipLevel` 1\u20134 (a new owner caps at 3).\n\n20. **`bulkWarning` \u2014 AssignBulkSignupWarning** [effect]\n    Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when > 80 owners already exist for that business day.\n\n21. **`possibleDuplicate` \u2014 AssignPossibleDuplicate** [effect]\n    Unless `sharesHousehold: true`, sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest (lowest-id) existing non-deleted owner sharing lastName (case-insensitive) and exact postcode; otherwise false/null.\n\n22. **`save` \u2014 SaveOwner** [effect]\n    Persists the owner (assigning its id).\n\n23. **`audit` \u2014 AuditOwnerCreated** [effect]\n    Emits an `AUDIT` log line: id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n\n24. **`recordIdempotency` \u2014 RecordIdempotentCreate** [effect]\n    If an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` so a later repeat replays (step 1).\n\n25. **`respond` \u2014 RespondWithOwnerCreated** [effect]\n    Maps to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**A couple of things worth flagging:**\n- Order matters for the status returned \u2014 field presence (400) is checked before the future-date/postcode format (400), before capacity (409) and daily limit (429), and both duplicate checks (409) run only after the derived `householdId`/`customerCode` exist.\n- Steps 12\u201321 are all derivations computed against the *current* `findAll()` snapshot before the new owner is saved, so each count/flag excludes the owner being created."
